        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I understand the problem better. The issue is in how `parseColumnNameList` works - it collects ALL column references including duplicates. Then in `ProjectionColumnProcessor.generateTransformExpressionKey()` and `TransformFilterProcessor.generateArguments()`, these duplicate column names get added to the argument lists, which causes Janino compilation to fail because Janino doesn't allow duplicate parameter names.\n\nThe fix needs to:\n1. Keep track of unique column names in the argument lists\n2. But still pass the correct values for each reference in the expression\n\nLet me check the test file to understand the expected behavior better:\n\n",
