          "text": "\n\nPerfect! The changes look good. Let me create a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented support for repeated column references in CDC transform rules (both projection and filter expressions). Here's what was changed:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File: `/workspace/flink-cdc-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/cdc/runtime/operators/transform/ProjectionColumnProcessor.java`**\n\n1. **`generateTransformExpressionKey()` method (lines 154-165)**: Added a check to skip duplicate column names when building the argument list for the Janino expression compiler. This prevents compilation failures due to duplicate parameter names.\n\n2. **`generateParams()` method (lines 99-137)**: Added tracking of already-added columns using a `List<String> addedColumns` to ensure each column value is only added once to the parameters array, matching the compiled expression signature.\n\n**File: `/workspace/flink-cdc-runtime/src/test/java/org/apache/flink/cdc/runtime/operators/transform/PostTransformOperatorTest.java`**\n\nAdded two new test methods to verify the fix:\n\n1. **`testRepeatedColumnReferenceInProjection()`**: Tests that a projection expression like `\"col1, col2, col2 * col2 AS square_col2\"` works correctly, producing the expected squared values.\n\n2. **`testRepeatedColumnReferenceInFilter()`**: Tests that a filter expression like `\"col2 < 3 OR col2 > 5\"` works correctly, allowing rows where col2 is 2 or 6 to pass through, but filtering out rows where col2 is 4.\n\n### How It Works\n\nThe fix ensures that when a column is referenced multiple times in an expression (e.g., `col2 * col2`):\n\n1. The Janino compiler receives only unique parameter names (avoiding compilation errors)\n2. The parameter values are correctly passed once per unique column\n3. The compiled expression can still reference the same parameter multiple times in the expression logic\n\nThis matches the existing behavior already implemented in `TransformFilterProcessor.generateArguments()`, which had the duplicate prevention logic, extending it to `ProjectionColumnProcessor` as well.\n\n### Test Results\n\n- All 16 PostTransformOperatorTest tests pass ✓\n- All 39 transform-related tests pass ✓\n- The new tests verify the exact scenario described in the requirements",
